# What `docker build ... apps/web` does not send to the builder.
#
# This file is the one that applies: the image is built with this directory as
# its context, and Docker reads the ignore file at the root of the context.
# The `.dockerignore` at the top of the repository is never consulted for it.
#
# The builder stage installs its own dependencies (`npm ci`) and then does
# `COPY . .`. Without this file that second step laid the workstation's own
# `node_modules` -- 750 MB, installed for whatever system the workstation is --
# over the clean install, and its stale `.next` beside it. CI never saw it: a
# fresh checkout has neither. An image built on a workstation is now built
# from what CI builds from (D240 in docs/roadmap.md).

# --- installed and built inside the image, never taken from the host --------
node_modules/
.next/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values reach the build as build arguments, not as files.
.env
.env.*

# --- output of running things here -------------------------------------------
build-output.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/
coverage/

# --- how the image is built ---------------------------------------------------
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.dev
.dockerignore

# --- editors / os --------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
